## Student flow: Homework only (don’t break)

**TEMPORARY:** Steps 2–4 are **fully removed** (code deleted). Flow is: **start → recording 1 → self-rate 1–10 → report** only. **Frontend must show the post-recording self-rate step** (e.g. "How was it? Rate 1–10") and call **POST .../self-rating** with `{ "rating": n }` before showing "Report generating" and polling for the report. To restore full flow: see `docs/TEMPORARY-REMOVED-STEPS-2-3-4-BACKUP.md` or git history.

**Single flow** under **`/v2/homework/...`**. Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <supabase_access_token>`.

**UX: Show recording right away.** On Homework page load: (1) `GET /v2/homework/session/status`. If `has_active_session` and `session`, render current step from `session.id` / `session.status`. (2) If no active session, call `POST /v2/homework/session/start` in same load (e.g. useEffect) and render warm-up task + record button immediately — no "Start homework" button. When **no active session**, status response may include **`assigned_exercises`**: `[ { id, title, video_url, description } ]` — **display these below the Start homework button** (videos from admin-assigned exercise; recognized in admin panel by title).

**Endpoints:**

1. **Start** — `POST /v2/homework/session/start`, body `{}` → `{ session_id, status: "warm_up", warm_up_task?: { id, text } }`. **Warm-up selection:** Currently first warm-up by `order_index` (`db.v2_get_assigned_warm_up_task`). Score-based `select_warm_up_task()` exists in `v2_flow_service` but is not wired; warm-ups have `max_performance_score` (0-1) for future use. **Frontend:** Render `warm_up_task.text`. If null, add warm-ups for student in admin.
2. **Warm-up (optional)** — `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/warm-up-task` → `{ warm_up_task }`.
3. **Recording 1** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-1` (multipart: `audio`; optional `duration_seconds`) → `{ recording_id, task_block: { metric_question_1, metric_question_2, metric_question_3 }, recording_1_processing }`. Background job sets `performance_score_1`, `context_short`, `recording_1_performance_profile` (pace_level, filler_level), `selected_task_id`. **Focus task selection:** Per-student `v2_focus_tasks` with score band (`max_performance_score >= performance_score_1`); excludes last 5 used tasks (from `v2_student_coaching_memory.recent_focus_task_ids`); when `recurring_issues` and task `targets` exist, multi-factor scorer (`score_and_pick_focus_task`) prefers tasks matching weaknesses (e.g. too_fast → pacing, high_fillers → fillers). Tasks can have `targets` JSONB (e.g. `["pacing"]`) and `difficulty`. **Frontend:** Show metric questions; collect `answer_1`, `answer_2`, `answer_3`; POST metric-answers. **Real-time glow (optional):** During recording, send PCM16 mono chunks to **POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-metrics-chunk** (binary body; headers X-Sample-Rate, X-Seq, X-T-Ms, X-Recording-Slot). Backend accepts 16k, 48k, or 44.1k (resamples to 16k internally). Pause-only: backend keeps 10 s rolling window per session; VAD 20 ms frames, pause events ≥200 ms; returns voiced_ratio, pause_score (1 = ideal). Brightness = function(pause_score). Silence-gated when voiced_ratio &lt; 0.15. Optional X-Debug for _debug (pause_ratio, pauses_per_min, max_pause_s). See **docs/REALTIME-METRICS-CONTRACT.md**. Rate limit 120/min per (user, session). Final upload still uses recording-1/recording-2 (WebM/Whisper).
4. **Metric answers** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/metric-answers`, body `{ answer_1, answer_2 }` → `{ final_task }`. **Final task:** AI-generated, exactly 2 sentences: (1) "Based on [context], your task is: [focus_task]." (2) "Focus especially on [metric_answer_1] and [metric_answer_2]." 20-50 words, no extra commentary. Status → `final_task_ready`.
5. **Recording 2** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/recording-2` (multipart) → `{ recording_id, performance_score_2 }`. Status → `post_questions`.
6. **Questions** — `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/questions` → `{ questions: [ ... ] }`. **Reflective questions:** Only if admin set exactly 3 `assigned_post_question_ids` for the student. Empty or not 3 → `questions: []` (skip step).
7. **Post-answers** — `POST /v2/homework/session/<id>/post-answers`, body `{ answers: [ { question_id, answer_text } ] }` → `{ report_text, performance_score_end, performance_metrics }`. **Report (homework):** 3 paragraphs (overview, metric analysis, next steps). Status → `completed`. **Coaching memory:** Right after marking session completed, `db.v2_upsert_student_coaching_memory(user_id, session_id)` updates `v2_student_coaching_memory`: `last_5_scores`, `recent_focus_task_ids`, and `recurring_issues` (derived from last 5 sessions’ `recording_1_performance_profile`: e.g. too_fast in ≥3 of 5 → `"too_fast"`).
8. **Status** — `GET /v2/homework/session/status` → `{ session | null, session_id?, has_active_session, tutor_feedback_deadline?, tutor_feedback_message? }`. Session may include **`tutor_video_url`** and **`tutor_video_description`** (see **`docs/FRONTEND-VIDEO-AND-DESCRIPTION.md`**). When no active session and the user recently completed a lesson (tutor hasn’t sent feedback yet), response includes **tutor_feedback_deadline** (ISO 8601) and **tutor_feedback_message** (user-facing string). **Frontend:** On the step 0 screen (no active session), show the **timer** (countdown to `tutor_feedback_deadline`) and **tutor_feedback_message** when present. **State to track for the timer:** show the timer whenever the status response includes **`tutor_feedback_deadline`**; hide it when that field is absent (e.g. after admin sends homework via POST send-assignment). See **`docs/APPLICATION-STATE.md`** §3.6. (Optional banner text: tutor_feedback_message, e.g. coach deadline “Your coach has until … to review your last lesson and send you new homework.”).

Session statuses (possible values; flow can skip): `warm_up`, `task_block`, `final_task_ready`, `post_questions`, `completing_from_recording_1`, `completed`. The student flow is **status-driven**, not a fixed 0→5 sequence: e.g. no focus tasks → after recording-1 status may be `report_generating` then `completed`; step 2 can skip to report via POST complete-from-recording-1; overrides can skip step 2 or 4.

**GET report:** `GET /v2/homework/session/<id>/report` returns 200 with report payload when session is `completed`. Payload includes `report_text`, `scores`, `final_recording` (playback), `performance_history` (chart), **`report_cta`** (e.g. "Send the homework to the coach!" — show at end of report as main CTA), and optionally **`recording`** (full `transcription_text`, `filler_words_count` { total, breakdown }, `audio_url`), **`context_short`**, **`coach_insight`** (2 AI sentences: context+fillers, progress+relevancy). **Frontend:** Show whole transcription, filler words used, recording playback, chart, coach_insight, and at the end **report_cta** (e.g. "Send the homework to the coach!"). When session is still generating, backend returns **409** with `REPORT_NOT_READY`; frontend should poll until 200. After the user leaves the report (e.g. clicks the CTA), they land on step 0; show the timer there when status includes **tutor_feedback_deadline** (see Status below).

